{"id": "clm:5dab387d900e1f854fb98866168a5e8d4a67a24d84e2b3e166f08c1c423e8bc9", "type": "statement", "text": "Builder classes and LINQ queries are not a security sanitization layer. Validate untrusted runtime field names and dictionary keys separately: the driver advisory describes keys being interpreted as path syntax while values are serialized as BSON values. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/crud/query/query-filter.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-csharp-driver/security/advisories/GHSA-2xqr-fxmx-2cmf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:186527611316a63c9194c2230bb87f4b7f777d8a1d7d5edc87723817e301b52c", "ev:712ab731d4cf004830bbe76052f8aff959d3c3ef9161ffcddf17b4dd0e5d8a49", "ev:95d5dea143babe06e110d0d4a2b3a75d990a1f1a18a840360911fef3f1b73fe0"]}
{"id": "clm:1397de3eed65c29bae777e287e7a36407ad67b7e0d2e6316c904d6499fddf908", "type": "statement", "text": "RegisterClassMap can explicitly define member mappings. Register a class map before it is needed; call AutoMap before adjusting individual members when combining automatic and manual mappings. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/serialization/class-mapping.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b6a3cca4846088a7c84a71cb95d9f988ebdb166fcc5317bb589ef3f0a7a3eb62", "ev:c7bdc1ed3d0b22cfed5c441cbdc0d0cfe47f2ccc98743bcb8d185a87ba80fda3", "ev:f0ac6c37838ac585af91ccbce2bd33f9e1ab08642ad207cf16bf4e0c61c2cf13"]}
{"id": "clm:96e8e31c8fde3d77f05a4ff384ed3b26b1544f2778f4a236f6d9cd257a490e67", "type": "statement", "text": "In Elsa issue 6001, the reporter traced an Expression not supported: x.Key failure during index creation to a read-only Key property omitted from the class map. The reporter proposed explicitly registering that property; this is a historical application report, not a universal current-driver failure. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/elsa-workflows/elsa-core/issues/6001", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:365ba3e18595c723520334395fcfd83e3f1fd8f042fd8457b699abfcbbaffc25", "ev:614375ee1a1bdeaa6f59a585796906b88d7818d5ef10f913e74f16ee0e8e7195", "ev:ca6ceadb4367bd26d912e4973751baf3e7865f9f5494e0a4c31f59183ca7338f", "ev:d4a8bd3b144243fbf28b8ab9faf153311aebc93b4484239b85d4d386fd475e9e"]}
{"id": "clm:e542846f5e4af7a717ddb2ef74269af15b57ad8ffe5916f3e347522fde0ab0ae", "type": "statement", "text": "Find supports FirstOrDefault and ToList materialization, including asynchronous forms. Fluent reads can chain Limit, Skip, SortBy, and Project. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/reference/quick-reference.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:15bb58222de7c7c424adea9bbda6450ea4aaef299fbb7a3adcaf768411008135", "ev:37ec3c641332caec6f09693b165b26e1cc878e10ef9dad8674db2a60231dd6f8", "ev:3ef9e833d90c75c393876206ce7bc4a9b2af16e31afcbc61795cee3c4830d442", "ev:6e37beaf4e09beb95d1836a06e0fb55b30216348ef920421211145edc2a9c859", "ev:71daa812936af6bb54b4b09d378547a338379277f0960cef136cae1b8f2a5560", "ev:8316d8799aaf1a6c4e18c9e8c2e9e795600042b00fadccd00182ad319b2ba232", "ev:b16e618b2b9c5f46ec5aedf30a8e286c633ec3a1dd9580a47ea867a6555fa0f1", "ev:d09f7793ef9cb37bb37338664eb44191fe983f364af1c0f3c8347aade87a0f71"]}
{"id": "clm:ef1f377e1d2d8c87334664da8c3b44eb7899d9673f08624bdbce58c0b8d39331", "type": "statement", "text": "Kevin Smith’s historical tutorial says LINQ lacks asynchronous methods. The official LINQ guide documents asynchronous iteration through ToAsyncEnumerable. Treat the tutorial’s async limitation as historical advice, not a universal constraint. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://kevsoft.net/2020/02/28/finding-documents-in-mongodb-using-csharp.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/aggregation/linq.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0c4046fd14600d958acc5fa2c3c4f94cae30524ce79f2b25df04873598177ae6", "ev:94959e1918598135ba9af66220ef28f58cea98c77843d784f2403f69d9cfb4df"]}
{"id": "clm:fe085b18ddd98db34a80230522f34d0f3a4f7bfb7f7ad92c26d7bf26936f0732", "type": "statement", "text": "Call AsQueryable() on a typed collection to compose LINQ queries; the driver translates supported LINQ expressions into aggregation operations rather than supporting every possible C# expression. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/aggregation/linq.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongodb-analyzer/current/code-type/linq.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7b16e7c9ec8ec5500d84b8fb735799be48b0445fa00ad86e494c3bcebe4d9279", "ev:e18ea7cc1d1349ae59fff3579017734e33bb29a5f18fcbe344ff8bc67592bb84", "ev:e67ed518818b7b79b2fa3157b312041f6026bf9fdf9625d6d69364d67c856094"]}
{"id": "clm:b91fb824e852baaf1a35d8035cd31f64c85f55c3d8457adec94cea0f36355898", "type": "statement", "text": "Query filters select documents for reads, updates and deletes; Builders<TDocument>.Filter provides builder methods for those filters. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/crud/query/query-filter.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6736ac4f98db4788d86db370b96d1b698a2506c633c60abcd40cc4ab19aea9b1"]}
{"id": "clm:75d666b7cbd1c51081f2760aefa47d77d1c02bb0d4d1c69bed4fb0af38daaf7a", "type": "statement", "text": "Typed equality filters can be passed to Find; the query-filter guide also shows the equivalent lambda predicate directly in Find. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/crud/query/query-filter.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/reference/quick-reference.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4881525582c1103ff8244e63fae3e77c65efb8c409d80ca2a8ed2a3e2f4d7904", "ev:5f8889644d3b87c8936c4271bde2d1b72df724091d1a101d4bd8f6911325df1b"]}
{"id": "clm:5372806f7c166f8b2a2a49413b2ac1f7bd005471ffc616c4aaa1745f5c020092", "type": "statement", "text": "The CRUD API exposes InsertOne and InsertMany for POCO documents, with asynchronous counterparts. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/reference/quick-reference.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9194f9cf7870f1184488c8907a95a751e4408dc313ad672a12a00ed9ddf74a72", "ev:c10be06645ce90663d2863d4b0cdf23730b9c90d09a4b1794207c14376b7e03d"]}
{"id": "clm:544013333656917d54dbeff768aad34a010fb0539d2ea74f7ca8f64d2930d4d6", "type": "statement", "text": "ReplaceOne accepts a replacement POCO and a filter; DeleteOne and DeleteMany accept filters, with asynchronous variants shown in the quick reference. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/reference/quick-reference.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ba85ef37aa2ec4ed0f901e7417f90e9508a70012c7402d45fb954d3be3b47d36"]}
{"id": "clm:67875e0856cade3edb5d0d12e86e55272ece735c9f260dbc0f74c9eba32f2ae1", "type": "statement", "text": "For LINQ diagnostics, ToString exposes the translated pipeline for non-scalar query objects. LoggedStages exposes it for scalar operations and must be read immediately after execution. LoggedStages is not thread-safe. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/aggregation/linq.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:33104f69a36e131e5103bce1bb4ccd52acb00e8a13424c8a78dcc7990781317b", "ev:37bb4c5a474530e8ade913128a3a543b2cf67828632a137e7028e843a3d3ddcb", "ev:73f5bb2f7bf7f9548475b7e0d796ca1b7b3fb4d650fa0be192dd824f925c1044"]}
{"id": "clm:2129e0b8fdb628f0507fdf5550411678b7a74fde2ebd967b821707d837493c66", "type": "statement", "text": "A POCO collection uses an automatic class map that matches document field names to class property names; incompatible property and field types can produce deserialization exceptions. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/serialization/class-mapping.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b6cd66dc4ce0850df2ed4126c423e86ba599f386282f202e07f17f281e0db68c"]}
{"id": "clm:ca56871ad6d8fa53876342b4a5f015df771c21eff55e89d3331b026647477130", "type": "statement", "text": "Typed collections can represent BSON documents as C# objects. The driver uses a class map to serialize and deserialize those objects. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/serialization/class-mapping.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://kevsoft.net/2020/02/28/finding-documents-in-mongodb-using-csharp.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0000820adedeb26d3549c134912ad925b1f2b885a9ce5db3702ac19d01ace41a", "ev:7b32f9b7a20005e10adb64734e58d6d2f4676be36f6000e278b3c214c4736c1b"]}
{"id": "clm:8c05a56dcae941be22c792161056927a6777aabe9613e3609ab0db58b7b55f58", "type": "statement", "text": "Filter builders and lambda predicates provide alternative ways to express equality queries passed to Find. Builder filters can also be composed conditionally. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/crud/query/query-filter.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://kevsoft.net/2020/02/28/finding-documents-in-mongodb-using-csharp.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5f8889644d3b87c8936c4271bde2d1b72df724091d1a101d4bd8f6911325df1b", "ev:77ce6a07154de7bf2e6a4a982e28837be70d0c106bca0b23a3370cdbb82aff10"]}
{"id": "clm:a7b5bd229bcaa79f92f59fef0c07984516e16ef68ccbe2662e6371d2ce27eabd", "type": "statement", "text": "An empty filter matches all documents. Query filters select the documents that read, update, and delete operations target. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/crud/query/query-filter.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3f19a71a4e6e67a628b15ce24550dd378c484fe8d6b173d3b674bb3c42415a07", "ev:6736ac4f98db4788d86db370b96d1b698a2506c633c60abcd40cc4ab19aea9b1"]}
{"id": "clm:f27a5280cb672f56e02a725cbc1806e1414816e6ccba7296e2b32458649aec2c", "type": "statement", "text": "Call AsQueryable on a collection to compose LINQ queries. The driver translates supported statements into aggregation pipeline stages, including Where into $match and Select into $project. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/aggregation/linq.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6a8b180a68f667afbd9012db9552d89dc79cdbb46adcb31c3c059c784b156120", "ev:88f365e8897e0f4dd276c08ab16c5b647323be8ed752ebfe37c08cb6eea708f8", "ev:896bec5b62caf93bf8a08b4c17b1bc187241ae2f464a8f0b63436206057da588", "ev:d369412d603b4cd7873e98f09a20193fed422d85c65ca49035094397eda6ebb7"]}
{"id": "clm:d2e884668238764273b27e5e3b2ccff238dc675896ae553432f544c1bdd83279", "type": "statement", "text": "Not every LINQ expression maps to a MongoDB query. The official guide lists unsupported Replace overloads that throw ExpressionNotSupportedException at runtime. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://kevsoft.net/2020/02/28/finding-documents-in-mongodb-using-csharp.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/aggregation/linq.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ccbca850aa3991b3e9c1a93ad6e6953aa490935961b71626033e4126e6586014", "ev:f15af980ab6f1fbe726abdc272c3723c37b4d39b110493f1608b518ebd82ef6f"]}
{"id": "clm:cf6f9a72bb9c8669d0acc07f1ccea553b339ea1faf7fd36bde2a1105dfc71d2e", "type": "statement", "text": "The version-three upgrade guide states that LINQ2 was removed and LINQ3 must be used for LINQ queries. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/reference/upgrade/v3.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0f8280814e0155c751e07ba11c6babce5dab614aa13e3dc547367d887bb94bb6"], "temporal": {"applicability_version": "3.x"}}
{"id": "clm:53d3592e70f0731f7294f3f47e7a2689c3aa73d318f060a426e7ae655da74567", "type": "statement", "text": "For client-side projections, the version-three upgrade guide documents ExpressionNotSupportedException by default and an opt-in through EnableClientSideProjections on TranslationOptions. These options can apply to an individual query or to MongoClientSettings. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/reference/upgrade/v3.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["C#/.NET driver CRUD with builders, LINQ provider and POCO mapping"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:fe1b510e21e80321619ebde045839c98be8d7ab36949e4e62a493fa4e634f481", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f02cfbb2a15d9da8edb65fe66673ff5298d336f6f5593429bd4d02e543132076"], "temporal": {"applicability_version": "3.x"}}
